<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shulgi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 2094–2047 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/21st-century-bce">21st century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shulgi was the second king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-dynasty-of-ur">Third Dynasty of Ur</a>, reigning c. 2094–2047 BCE. He reorganised the administration, created standard weights and measures and a provincial system, and expanded the realm through military campaigns. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/neo-sumerian-empire">Neo-Sumerian Empire</a> profile presents his reign as the height of the empire.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/shulgi.jpg" alt="Shulgi" width="320" height="168" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ward, William Hayes, 1835-1916 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Shulgi_seal_(drawing).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
